  "For Canada, the Governor-General, who represents the Monarch, is given as Head of State, and the Prime Minister as Head of Government. For the United Kingdom, the Monarch as Head of State, and the Prime Minister as Head of Government.": "audio/en/510f0bd1bc7afb26.mp3",
  "For Switzerland and for the United States, only one of the two is named. In each of them the President is given as the Head of the Government — though the American President is, in fact, Head of State as well.": "audio/en/9da1488a585a5309.mp3",
  "India's key features: a multi-party democracy, a written constitution, Fundamental Rights and Duties, and federalism.": "audio/en/dbff0538ee1d0b5f.mp3",
  "The Monarch is the Head of State, and the Prime Minister the Head of Government. The United Kingdom's key features: an unwritten constitution, parliamentary sovereignty, and a multi-party system.": "audio/en/88f36d97df44d683.mp3",
  "Switzerland is a direct democracy. Executive power lies with the Federal Council, and the President, who chairs the Federal Council for one year at a time, is the Head of the Government.": "audio/en/ab2f27a7d2d61fdf.mp3",
  "The United States of America is a representative democracy — a presidential democracy. Executive power lies with the President, who is both the Head of State and the Head of the Government.": "audio/en/06aeb151ba7c7489.mp3",
